e, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<b>Phrasal verbs</b> are verbs that have a preposition that changes the meaning of the verb. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Phrasal verbs</b> are commonly used in English language. Whether it is in formal or informal conversations, they make up an important part of language usage.<br/><br/>  Most <strong>phrasal verbs</strong> can only take one preposition, but there are some that can take up to two or three prepositions, each conveying a different meaning. We can also classify <b>phrasal verbs</b> into separable or inseparable, meaning that the object can go between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition.<br/><br/>  Verbs working with different prepositions may have a different meaning from the verb when used with no preposition.<br/><br/>  Let's take a look at some <b>phrasal verbs</b> are:<br/> <ul> <li><b>Pick out</b>: to choose from a wide variety</li> <li><b>Count on</b>: to have the support of someone or something</li> <li><b>Work something over</b>: to do something again</li> <li><b>Rely on</b>: to trust something or someone</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are different types of operators people can pick out to perform a given action in JavaScript. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is always a good idea to count on a reference chart if you're new at JavaScript.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This will save you a lot of time instead of having to work something over.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Bitwise Operators in JavaScript", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<b>Bitwise operators</b> are operations that work in binary code, that is to say, with a combination of zeros and ones. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <b>bitwise operators</b> allow a different organization of operands. The bitwise AND, OR, XOR, and NOT work as an operational logic between operands. Those operators run the operations in each bit or pairs of bits, or alike.<br/><br/>  On the other hand, the shift <b>bitwise operators</b> reorganize the operands to interact in different ways following bit-by-bit operations.<br/><br/>  The <b>bitwise operators</b> are:<br/> <ul> <li>Bitwise AND</li> <li>Bitwise OR</li> <li>Bitwise XOR</li> <li>Bitwise Not</li> <li>Left shift</li> <li>Right shift</li> <li>Right shift with zero</li> </ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "go deeper ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to explore something with more detail or to get to the bottom of a situation  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before we go deeper into the operators topic, there are some things that should be cleared out beforehand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "beforehand ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "with anticipation, before a given event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before we go deeper into the operators topic, there are some things that should be cleared out beforehand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comprise ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to compose, cover or include ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Assignment operators that comprise the \u2018simple assignment', \u2018add and assignment', \u2018subtract and assignment', and others, assign a value to the left operand taking into account the value of the right operand. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "output ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the result or final product  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In case you can't get the expected output, you can rely on online tutorials or an experienced person to get you out of trouble.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spelling ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "synonym of orthography, how something is written ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Make sure your spelling is correct to avoid typos and misplaced symbols.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "work something over ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something again  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This will save you a lot of time instead of having to work something over.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for information about JavaScript operators. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create some flashcards where you include the type of operators and some examples. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one of the operators and prepare a presentation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand what operators in JavaScript are. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list the types of operators. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe the characteristics of operators in JavaScripts. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}]}